Compare dynamic models up to isomorphism

Provide checked model homomorphisms and isomorphism witnesses on
equality classes so evaluation strategies can be compared despite
different element allocation and index layouts. Support comparison
under a common base even when its elements become identified during
evaluation.

Normalize relation tuples without mutating models or running rules.
Use joint color refinement and backtracking to find type-preserving
bijections that preserve and reflect all relations, including function
graphs and membership. Keep homomorphisms tied to immutable model
borrows so their validation cannot become stale.
